<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's near-term PHIBOR fall, others steady.</title>
<headline>Manila's near-term PHIBOR fall, others steady.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were weaker at the short end of the curve, while the longer-term maturities remained unchanged, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A trader said banks adjusted their rates after overnight rates fell on ample liquidity in the system.</p>
<p>The steady longer-termed rates can be attributed to the stable long-term outlook in the domestic interest rates, he added.</p>
<p>PHIBOR are the average foreign exchange forward rates quoted by 20 banks.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 OCT 15		  OCT 14</p>
<p>    1 W		11  5/8		 11 3/4</p>
<p>    2 W		11  9/16		11 11/16</p>
<p>    1 M		11  1/2		 11 5/8</p>
<p>    2 M		11  1/2		 11 1/2</p>
<p>    3 M		11  9/16		11 9/16</p>
<p>    6 M		11  3/4		 11 3/4</p>
<p>    12M		11  7/8		 11 7/8</p>
<p>    VAL		16-Oct		  15-Oct</p>
<p>- RAMONCITO DELA CRUZ 63 2 8109636 Fax 8176267</p>
